.TH LAZYFINDER 1 "2026-10-13" "lazyfinder" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
lazyfinder \- a Finder-like file manager for the terminal
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lazyfinder
[\fIflags\fR] [\fIdirectory\fR]
.br
.B lazyfinder \-\-follow
\fIdirectory\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
lazyfinder shows a folder as a list or as columns (parent, folder, preview), with a sidebar, tabs, previews,
search, tags, an Open With menu and mouse support. It starts in \fIdirectory\fR, or in the current folder.
Everything is configurable in \fIconfig.json\fR; press \fB,\fR inside the program for the settings.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-print\-default\-config
Print the default config.json and exit.
.TP
.BI \-\-log " file"
Write a JSON log to \fIfile\fR (off by default).
.TP
.B \-\-log\-paths
Include file names in the log.
.TP
.BI \-\-lang " language"
Interface language for this run: auto, en, es, pt, fr, de, it, ja or zh.
.TP
.BI \-\-theme " name"
Theme for this run: a built-in or user theme, or \fBterminal\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-follow " directory"
Follow a project in a narrow tree with live updates and git state.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-mouse
Ignore the mouse for this run.
.TP
.BI \-\-completions " shell"
Print the completion script of \fIshell\fR (bash, zsh or fish) and exit.
.TP
.BI \-\-cwd\-file " file"
On exit, write the folder lazyfinder ends in to \fIfile\fR, unless \fBcd_on_exit\fR is false.
.TP
.BI \-\-shell\-init " shell"
Print the function of \fIshell\fR (bash, zsh or fish) that runs lazyfinder with \fB\-\-cwd\-file\fR and leaves
the shell in that folder, and exit: \fBeval "$(lazyfinder \-\-shell\-init zsh)"\fR in \fI~/.zshrc\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-herdr " action"
A step of the herdr plugin (\fIherdr\-plugin.toml\fR) and exit: \fBensure\fR docks a sidebar in the tab of the
event, \fBtoggle\fR opens, focuses or closes it. It runs inside herdr, which sets \fBHERDR_SOCKET_PATH\fR.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/lazyfinder/config.json
Settings, keys, openers and custom commands. \fBLAZYFINDER_CONFIG\fR overrides the path.
.TP
.I recents.json, searches.json, tags.json
Kept next to config.json.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Turns colors off.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 on a runtime error, 2 on a usage error.
.SH SEE ALSO
Keys: docs/keybindings.md. Settings: docs/configuration.md.
